          {
           "type": "sub",
           "text": "How to Map Drives to a User’s PC"
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 1,
           "text": "Add the User to the relevant Group based on the request."
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 2,
           "text": "If the Drive does not automatically show up, open File Explorer"
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 3,
           "text": "Right-click “This PC” then “Map Network Drive”"
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 4,
           "text": "Choose the proper Drive Letter based on the table above, and add the path based on the path listed in the table"
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 5,
           "text": "Make sure “Reconnect at sign-in” is enabled"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "tab": "New User setup",
         "blocks": [
          {
           "type": "sub",
           "text": "Onboarding Process - Active Directory"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Have the hiring manager/original ticket creator fill in the New User Request Form."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Make sure that the user provides as much detail as possible. This includes any other third-party applications, distribution lists, security groups, etc."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Determine if the user is created in Admin 365 or in Active Directory. If the user is created in AD always perform changes on AD even if the same options exist in Admin 365 (example: resetting passwords)."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Create the new user in the proper folder (this can either be a general “Users” folder or a folder specifically for their department)."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "For the reserve club, the name format is:"
          },
          {
           "type": "indent",
           "text": "[first initial].[last name]@the reserveclub.com\nJohn Doe → john.doe@the reserveclub.com"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "If applicable, you can use a departing user as a template for the new user (ask the ticket creator beforehand). Add the user’s job title in “Description” if other users in the company have their job title listed as well."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "When creating a user, make sure to use the @thereserveclub.com email, never .local unless stated otherwise. In “Attributes”, under proxyaddress, add the user’s new email address:"
          },
          {
           "type": "indent",
           "text": "Example: SMTP:john.doe@thereserveclub"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Add the new user into the relevant share folders and security groups that the ticket creator did not add in the New User Request Form. Use the DeltaSync file located in the Desktop to push the newly created user."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Make sure to use the Secret Sharing system from Club Support when sending passwords!"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "https://csms.clubsupportinc.com/secrets"
          },
          {
           "type": "sub",
           "text": "Onboarding Process - Microsoft 365"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Log in to Microsoft 365 with the csupport@thereserveclub.com account."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Find the newly created user and under Licenses, grant the license (if any) requested by the ticket creator, which should be outlined in the New User Request Form. If a license is required, send an email to “Licenses@clubsupportinc.com” under this format:\n\n Subject: Add (1/2/etc.) license to the reserve club"
          },
          {
           "type": "indent",
           "text": "Body:\n\nLicense is for:\n\nUser Requesting License (username@thereserveclub.com)\nExchange Online/Business Standard Monthly/monthly Commit\nRequested by:\nManager/Controller\t\tTicket No."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Depending on the club, mailbox delegation, distribution lists, and other 365-exclusive groups should also be assigned in Exchange. To do so, go to “Exchange”, then depending on the mailbox, grant the proper permissions. For example, if you want to delegate the shared mailbox “Catering” to the user, go to the catering mailbox, and add the new user under the “Read and Manage” permissions."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Outlook usually adds the inbox to the user’s mailbox automatically, but if this doesn’t occur, you can add the mailbox manually in Outlook. To do this, right-click the account name in the left folder pane, select Add shared folder or mailbox, enter the mailbox address."
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "tab": "User disable",
         "blocks": [
          {
           "type": "sub",
           "text": "Offboarding Process - Active Directory"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Club Support Policy dictates that we rarely, if ever delete accounts in systems once created. Permissions and security group memberships in AD are generally left intact."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Reset the password to ensure that the user cannot sign-in with their previous credentials. Afterwards, right click the user to be offboarded, and press “Disable” if requested. If any changes are done, make sure to run the DeltaSync script on the desktop."
          },
          {
           "type": "sub",
           "text": "Offboarding Process - Microsoft 365"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "The offboarding process differs from club to club, so double check the ticket as the creator will usually include what needs to be taken off and what needs to be retained"
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Log in to the 365 portal with csupport@countryhills.ab.ca and find the user to be offboarded. To disallow the user from signing back in, press both “Block Sign-in” and “Sign Out Of All Sessions” to remove the user."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "To unlicense a user, go to “Licenses” and remove their Microsoft 365 Basic/Standard license to remove their Outlook and Word license. If the license isn’t immediately being transferred to another user, you can remove the license by emailing Licenses@clubsupportinc.com"
          },
          {
           "type": "indent",
           "text": "Subject: Remove (1/2/etc.) license in The Reserve Club\nBody:\n\nLicense is for:\n\nDeparting User (username@thereserveclub.com)\nExchange Online/Business Standard Monthly/monthly Commit\nRequested by:\nManager/Controller\t\tTicket No."
          },
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "In Exchange, go to the user to be offboarded, and convert their mailbox into a shared mailbox. If Read Access, Send, or Send As access is requested by the ticket creator, this is also done in Exchange. Email forwarding is also done in Exchange if requested by the ticket creator."
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "tab": "Proper Server Shutdown and Startup Procedure",
         "blocks": [
          {
           "type": "p",
           "text": "Consult with Yurii/Stan and any managers before doing any server shutdowns and startups. They are in charge of the regularly scheduled server reboots for most of the clubs. If they are unavailable, contact Kosta as we do not reboot servers without prior consent. If a shutdown is required, here is a general guideline to maintain connectivity:"
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 1,
           "text": "Notify users and departments of the downtime and provide an accurate timeframe on when services can be fully up and running again."
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 2,
           "text": "Schedule the downtime after hours (Usually 10:00 PM to 4:00 AM local time) to prevent any issues in the future."
          },
          {
           "type": "step",
           "num": 3,
           "text": "Shutdown and/or restart the servers as required and log everything that occurs."
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
